# Fast Flights API Patterns

## Query Building
Always use the structured query API from [querying.py](mdc:fast_flights/querying.py):

```python
from fast_flights import FlightQuery, Passengers, create_query, get_flights

# Preferred: Structured queries
query = create_query(
    flights=[
        FlightQuery(
            date="2025-12-22",
            from_airport="TPE", 
            to_airport="MYJ"
        )
    ],
    seat="economy",
    trip="one-way", 
    passengers=Passengers(adults=1),
    language="en-US"
)
result = get_flights(query)
```

## Data Models
Use dataclasses from [model.py](mdc:fast_flights/model.py) for type safety:
- `FlightQuery` - Individual flight requests
- `Passengers` - Passenger configuration  
- `Query` - Complete search query
- `Airport`, `Airline`, `Alliance` - Reference data
- `Flights`, `SingleFlight` - Response data

## Protocol Buffers
- Protocol buffer definitions are in [pb/flights.proto](mdc:fast_flights/pb/flights.proto)
- Generated Python code is in [pb/flights_pb2.py](mdc:fast_flights/pb/flights_pb2.py)
- Always use `.pb()` methods to convert to protobuf format
- Base64 encode for Google Flights URL parameters

## Integrations
- Base integration class is in [integrations/base.py](mdc:fast_flights/integrations/base.py)
- Implement `fetch_html()` method for custom integrations
- BrightData integration example in [integrations/bright_data.py](mdc:fast_flights/integrations/bright_data.py)

## Error Handling
- Always handle network errors gracefully
- Use optional parameters for non-essential data
- Validate passenger counts (max 9 total, infants_on_lap ≤ adults)